  "adventure.wonder.door": "Office Wonderland",
  "adventure.wonder.keys": "Keys: {n}/{m}",
  "adventure.wonder.hint": "Through the looking-glass every card acts as its opposite: the Ace plays as a 2, the King as a 3, the Queen as a 4, and so on. Your ult charges off THEIR cards. Richer chests. One pass.",
  "adventure.wonder.leave": "Leave",
  "adventure.wonder.leave.title": "Leaving the mirror?",
  "adventure.wonder.leave.body": "The door closes behind you: the pass ends here and its keys stay spent. The chapter itself is waiting where you left it.",
  "adventure.wonder.how": "Every boss you fell on this floor drops one key. {m} of them open the door \u2014 you have {n}.",
  "adventure.wonderTitle": "Looking-Glass {n}",
  "adventure.story.wonder.title": "Through the Looking-Glass",
  "adventure.story.wonder.body": "The floor is the same floor. The desks stand where they stood. Only everything on them is the wrong way round, and nobody here thinks that is worth mentioning.\n\nThe deck is read from the other end: the Ace strikes like a 2, a 2 like the Ace, the King like a 3, the Queen like a 4. Only the 8 stays itself, having nowhere to mirror to. Your ult charges off THEIR cards, not yours. The chests are richer, and the door behind you is already gone: one pass, until the boss falls.",
  // Short version — what the door shows on the way in. The full text stays behind the "i" button.
  "adventure.story.wonder.short": 'The deck reads from the other end: an ace hits like a two, a king like a three. Your ult charges off THEIR cards.\n\nOne pass, until the boss falls. Details under "i".',
  "adventure.story.wonder.line": '"Mind the mirror. It minds you back."',
