  // Chapter opening story — auto-shown on first entry to a chapter, re-openable via the "i" button.
  // Hybrid form: `.body` is the narrator's paragraph, `.line` is ONE spoken line from the chapter's face
  // (rendered under the chapter's bossAvatar portrait). Keep `.line` short — it wraps beside a 96px head.
  "adventure.story.next": "Next",
  "adventure.story.go": "Onward!",
  "adventure.story.ch1.title": "Down the Rabbit-Hole",
  "adventure.story.ch1.body": "Your brother stepped into the revolving door at a quarter past nine and never came out the other side. Nobody at reception thought it worth writing down.",
  "adventure.story.ch1.line": "\u201CBelow the lobby? There is no below the lobby. Badge, please \u2014 and mind you are not counted twice.\u201D",
  "adventure.story.ch2.title": "The Pool of Tears",
  "adventure.story.ch2.body": "Somebody has cried a whole quarter into the open space. The printers weep ink, the desks drift, and an intern paddles by on a drawer, apologising for the wake.",
  "adventure.story.ch2.line": "\u201CMind the tide \u2014 too many cards, then too few. Nobody keeps their dignity treading paperwork. You only keep your desk.\u201D",
  "adventure.story.ch3.title": "A Caucus-Race",
  "adventure.story.ch3.body": "The agenda has one item, and the item is the agenda. The clock gave up long ago; its hands are kept on for decoration.",
  "adventure.story.ch3.line": "\u201CThe motion carries: round we go again. Nobody leaves till somebody wins \u2014 and here everybody always has, with prizes. Beat me properly, or take a prize and stay.\u201D",
  "adventure.story.ch4.title": "The Rabbit Sends in a Little Bill",
  "adventure.story.ch4.body": "HR was expecting you. There is a folder with your name on it, and a thinner one with your brother\u2019s, stamped TRANSFERRED, which you are not to read.",
  "adventure.story.ch4.line": "\u201CSign here. And here. If the room shrinks around you, that is the room\u2019s business \u2014 and your brother\u2019s folder stays shut.\u201D",
  "adventure.story.ch5.title": "Advice from a Caterpillar",
  "adventure.story.ch5.body": "The Consultant sits on a stool shaped like a mushroom. You explain yourself twice, and he is satisfied neither time.",
  "adventure.story.ch5.line": "\u201CAnd who are you? No \u2014 say it the other way. One side of that answer makes you taller, the other shorter. Win, and I shall tell you which floor took your brother.\u201D",
  "adventure.story.ch6.title": "Pig and Pepper",
  "adventure.story.ch6.body": "There is far too much pepper in this pantry. The microwaves shriek, the fridge has been keeping something since spring, and the Chef throws whatever comes to hand, on principle.",
  "adventure.story.ch6.line": "\u201CToo much pepper? There is exactly enough. Everything lands harder down here \u2014 my ladle, your cards, the sneezing. Stairs are behind the fridge, piglet.\u201D",
  // "?" points explainer — what each map node does.
